---
layout: default
page_class: "course webinar selling"
title: "When the Cloud Savings Stop"
social_title: "When the Cloud Savings Stop | A free webinar from Lee Atchison"
description: "Why the finance playbook stops finding money, and the design decisions that set the rest of your cloud bill. A free 30-minute session for architects and engineering leaders."
# 1200x630 link preview: the webinar's "Webinar Event Cover 1920x1080.png"
# with its date replaced by the short URL, so it never goes stale between
# runs (Lee, 2026-10-03). Source: assets_inbox/webinar-architecting-for-cost-preview-1920x1080.png.
image: /images/webinars/architecting-for-cost-og.png
# Supporting page (Spec0031 §B5), same pattern as architecting-with-ai.erb.
# Copy: Dropbox webinar-architecting-for-cost/Marketing/Webinar Page Copy.md
# (copied to assets_inbox/webinar-architecting-for-cost-page-copy.md).
#
# ⚠️ NEVER MOVE OR RENAME THIS FILE. The short link /cost-webinar (a 302 in
# netlify.toml) points at /webinars/architecting-for-cost/, and that short
# link is spoken in a recorded video and shown on its last slide.
#
# PER-RUN SETTINGS. Everything else on the page stays the same every run.
#   state:              upcoming (before a run) or replay (after it)
#   starts_at:          the run's date and time, shown exactly as written
#   linkedin_event_url: the run's LinkedIn Event; blank shows "registration
#                       opens soon" instead of the button
#   replay_url:         the replay video (Vimeo or YouTube), embedded on the
#                       unlisted replay page, webinars/architecting-for-cost/replay/
#                       (WEB-19). This page never links to it directly.
#   replay_kit_form_uid: the Kit form "Webinar replay: When the Cloud Savings
#                       Stop" (the data-uid in Kit's embed code), shown in
#                       state: replay. Kit sends the replay link. While it is
#                       KIT_FORM_ID_PENDING (or blank) the page shows a marked
#                       placeholder, and a production build in state: replay
#                       fails, so the form can't go live without its id.
#   offer_slug:         the run's offer page (e.g. launch). While that offer
#                       is live and active, the offer block shows its price,
#                       end date and Buy button; otherwise it shows the
#                       standard price and links to the sales page.
state: replay
starts_at: "Thursday, November 19, 10am Pacific"
linkedin_event_url: "https://www.linkedin.com/events/7512578068063125504/"
replay_url: "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/SRvfyylYqJ0"
replay_kit_form_uid: "KIT_FORM_ID_PENDING"
product: architecting-for-cost
offer_slug: launch
---

<%
  unless %w[upcoming replay].include?(data.state)
    raise "#{resource.relative_path}: state: #{data.state} must be upcoming or replay"
  end
  sales = site.data.sales[data.product]
  offer = current_offer(data.product, data.offer_slug)
  offer_page = offer && selling_page(offer)
  form_uid = data.replay_kit_form_uid.to_s.strip
  form_ready = form_uid != "" && form_uid != "KIT_FORM_ID_PENDING"
  if data.state == "replay" && !form_ready &&
     Bridgetown.env.production? && ENV["CONTEXT"] != "deploy-preview"
    raise "#{resource.relative_path}: replay_kit_form_uid is still a placeholder — " \
          "put the real Kit form uid in before state: replay goes live"
  end
%>

<section class="course-header">
  <div class="course-header-inner webinar-hero">
    <div class="webinar-hero-text">
      <div class="course-badge-row">
        <span class="course-platform-badge">Free webinar</span>
      </div>
      <h1><%= data.title %></h1>
      <div class="webinar-intro">
        <p>Your company tagged everything, shrank the oversized servers, and bought reserved capacity. It found real money.</p>
        <p>Then the savings stopped, and the bill kept climbing.</p>
      </div>

      <%# The webinar block: the part that changes between runs. %>
      <% if data.state == "upcoming" %>
        <p class="webinar-date-line"><%= data.starts_at %> &middot; 30 minutes &middot; Free on LinkedIn Live</p>
        <div class="webinar-actions">
          <% if data.linkedin_event_url.to_s != "" %>
            <%# LinkedIn is third-party, so it opens in a new tab. %>
            <a href="<%= data.linkedin_event_url %>" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Save your seat on LinkedIn</a>
          <% else %>
            <p class="webinar-pending">Registration opens soon on LinkedIn. Check back here for the link.</p>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <p class="webinar-date-line">Recorded webinar &middot; free to watch</p>
        <%# The replay gate (WEB-19): an email form in place of a direct link.
            Kit draws the field and the "Send me the replay" button, and shows
            the success message in place; both are set on the form in Kit.
            index.js fires the Fathom event once that message appears. The
            note under the form must show before submit (Lee, 2026-11-12). %>
        <div class="webinar-replay-form">
          <p class="webinar-replay-lead"><strong>Get the replay by email.</strong> Enter your email and I'll send you the link.</p>
          <% if form_ready %>
            <div class="sales-kit-form" data-kit-form data-fathom-event="webinar-replay-signup">
              <script async data-uid="<%= form_uid %>" src="https://softwarearchitectureinsights.kit.com/<%= form_uid %>/index.js"></script>
            </div>
          <% else %>
            <p class="selling-placeholder">Replay signup form not configured yet: set <code>replay_kit_form_uid</code> in this page's front matter.</p>
          <% end %>
          <p class="webinar-form-note">I'll send the link, plus a note about the course. You'll also join my weekly newsletter, Software Architecture Insights. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%# The illustration from the event cover, without its text (cut from
        assets_inbox/webinar-architecting-for-cost-event-cover-1920x1080.png). %>
    <img class="webinar-hero-art" src="<%= relative_url '/images/webinars/architecting-for-cost-art.jpg' %>"
         width="1060" height="530" alt="A hand pressing down on a concrete floor, with a glowing gem in a hollow beneath it" />
  </div>
</section>

<section class="course-body">
  <div class="course-body-inner">
    <h2>Below the floor</h2>
    <p>Every team that runs the finance playbook hits a floor. Above it was waste. Below it is something else.</p>
    <p>Everything below the floor was set by design decisions. How many services you run. Where your data moves. How fast you need to recover.</p>
    <p>In this session you'll see:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Why tagging, rightsizing and commitments all stop at the same place</li>
      <li>How to read your cloud bill backwards, from a line item to the decision that caused it</li>
      <li>What one small system costs at each recovery target, from $413 to $1,270 a month</li>
      <li>Where finance's job ends and yours begins</li>
      <li>Three things you can do Monday</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Who it's for:</strong> Architects, senior engineers and engineering leaders who own a cloud cost target.</p>

    <%# About Lee: the sales page's block, minus its last paragraph (which is
        about the course), from the same sales data file. %>
    <% about = sales.about %>
    <div class="sales-about webinar-about">
      <img src="<%= relative_url about.photo %>" width="<%= about.photo_width %>" height="<%= about.photo_height %>"
           alt="Lee Atchison" class="sales-about-photo" />
      <div>
        <h2><%= about.heading %></h2>
        <% about.paragraphs[0...-1].each do |para| %>
          <p><%= sales_text para, sales %></p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# The offer block: changes with the run's offer (offer_slug). %>
    <%= render "webinars/offer", sales: sales, offer: offer, offer_page: offer_page %>

    <%= render "webinars/worksheet" %>

    <%# The same every run. Both links open a new tab (Lee, 2026-10-03). %>
    <h2>Have a question?</h2>
    <p>Ask me. I'll get back to you.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://leeatchison.com/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contact me</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leeatchison/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Message me on LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
